#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:41
#: a3ae8ed4d6684c12821f85898f7bd9c3
msgid "AutoPilot Basic Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:42
#: 80814163f94a43bab31c15274be61519
msgid "To enable Ethernet on the autopilot the following parameters are set (other NET params stay at default) and reboot the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:44
#: 6cbe8bad3e2a46b0a7fb79eef3adc8b6
msgid ":ref:`NET_ENABLE<NET_ENABLE>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:46
#: 383d95bb655448278faa31e870c21c3c
msgid "then set the autopilot's IP address, it must be in the 192.168.144.x to be in the Herelink's listening range..this will drive other addresses to be set later also:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:48
#: 673c4ac51ada4f90ba4f28c7a7a94401
msgid ":ref:`NET_IPADDR0<NET_IPADDR0>` = 192"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:49
#: 693ec0e8556249c2b77b3f22da820f10
msgid ":ref:`NET_IPADDR1<NET_IPADDR1>` = 168"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:50
#: 2edda908a57f4571b554303e26fd28ee
msgid ":ref:`NET_IPADDR2<NET_IPADDR2>` = 144"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:51
#: 958b9234bae342aeb98cf686e8197b95
msgid ":ref:`NET_IPADDR3<NET_IPADDR3>` = 26 <- arbitrarily chosen but must not be 11 (Herelink fixed address)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:52
#: cc20284fdef6434f9248b082af3d9071
msgid ":ref:`NET_NETMASK<NET_NETMASK>` = 24 <- this says we are in a subnet with addresses 192.168.144.1 to 192.168.144.254"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:54
#: 0ca9d94f30a64e69b94b9b1338d1207d
msgid "if the autopilot needs to communicate with IP addresses outside this range it will use a \"gateway\" in the subnet...we won't be doing this but it still needs to be set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:56
#: 93c1441cc34348d0b77cb6faf9831e2e
msgid ":ref:`NET_GWADDR0<NET_GWADDR0>` = 192"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:57
#: 80fde90e323c4540a7eec1e96772cef2
msgid ":ref:`NET_GWADDR1<NET_GWADDR1>` = 168"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:58
#: ee55791b8bff4729b4e214bab6ad0158
msgid ":ref:`NET_GWADDR2<NET_GWADDR2>` = 144"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:59
#: f7d0bfdbadaa46beba898d026344c78b
msgid ":ref:`NET_GWADDR3<NET_GWADDR3>` = 1 <- typical address of subnet gateway"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:61
#: e1afe5b11b4b4de4838ed18c82ecaf62
msgid "Now basic Ethernet for the autopilot is enabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:64
#: c8e1700cd1fb4099970cf02eb8791a47
msgid "Gimbal Camera Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:65
#: e4a7d37b90a34e87b96e1982a790043d
msgid "Set :ref:`CAM1_TYPE<CAM1_TYPE>` = 4 to allow camera control of shutter, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:67
#: 8690c392fd59415f81cc99fe7364980f
msgid "The gimbal/camera must be set up to use the Ethernet for video streaming and its IP param setup. To do this download the `SIYI Assistant <https://siyi.biz/en/index.php?id=downloads&asd=22>`__ and use it to set the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:72
#: c07dc81088ae41ac80ac2bb9a537d161
msgid "save and power cycle the gimbal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:74
#: bc9f669600714c639a2d292122aff5f5
msgid "This sets the gimbal's IP address within the Herelink's listening range for passthru to the ground controller to display video and sets its video output to Ethernet with an H.264 encoded stream that the ground station can decode. Now the camera will be streaming video over Ethernet, through the switch, and the Herelink air unit will transmit it down to the ground controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:76
#: faeab0ef3b3847e9b5a0b6dbbd58e6bf
msgid "As of this writing, the SIYI A8 camera has about 1 second image latency over Ethernet which makes its use for realtime FPV guidance not viable. I also have a mini HDMI cable attached from the SIYI HDMI port to the Herelink's HDMI1 input and switch the source in the SIYI Assistant to HDMI rather than Ethernet (source = \"Close\") when I actually fly. Other gimbals from SIYI or others may or may not have this issue. Also the Herelink Air Unit uses better bandwidth management if the HDMI input is used. But the setup illustrates the method for use in other device combinations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:79
#: e82df416afdc4a8d9d0796ca93400895
msgid "Gimbal Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:81
#: f6a260cc2055487f91db5bf626a5c3cf
msgid "Control of the gimbal (pan/tilt/camera start/stop,etc.) over Ethernet is obtained from the autopilot which interprets MAVLink commands (also AUX switch inputs) and sends them to the gimbal. First, we must set up ArduPilot to control the Mount/Camera:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:83
#: 4f15fee5160a4654975dc681d5999918
msgid ":ref:`MNT1_TYPE<MNT1_TYPE>` = 8 This selects the SIYI mount type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:85
#: 51968b394605414bb364671af5585116
msgid "then reboot to see all the MNT params and set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:87
#: c31367c31f254eb0b84d41472c6619cd
msgid ":ref:`MNT1_YAW_MAX<MNT1_YAW_MAX>` = 135"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:88
#: 67c51985e6184f42ac750f2d42987a90
msgid ":ref:`MNT1_YAW_MIN<MNT1_YAW_MIN>` = -135"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:90
#: 352f441efe1f428faa749fd4782cf0d5
msgid "which is the limit of the yaw that SIYI can accommodate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:92
#: 61e898b740cc4003868bd2f7793e8d3e
msgid "Then we need to set up an Ethernet mechanism to communicate. Using the NET_P1 params we will create a \"virtual\" serial port to talk to the mount/camera, just as if we were using a UART (which the SIYI could also use instead of Ethernet control, but why add wires?). Set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:94
#: 7708a2d5c4fd4d6dbe6e6de288b25411
msgid ":ref:`NET_P1_TYPE<NET_P1_TYPE>` = 1 <- UDP Client type of port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:96
#: 02a646c48f6a43bd9b1fddf2619d32ad
msgid "reboot for the params to show:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:98
#: 4500dccaf406473e9c3c6f64db6965bd
msgid ":ref:`NET_P1_IP0<NET_P1_IP0>` = 192"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:99
#: 8f943fc6b8b64b3c8ea513f3d0d6b4e0
msgid ":ref:`NET_P1_IP1<NET_P1_IP1>` = 168"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:100
#: 42fac00f2e1847ecbeecc2099bbf6bcd
msgid ":ref:`NET_P1_IP2<NET_P1_IP2>` = 144"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:101
#: 5d7dadb17af340629bdde30aa8bcc395
msgid ":ref:`NET_P1_IP3<NET_P1_IP3>` = 25   <- the IP address we set for the Gimbal previously"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:102
#: 2cda138e4c9f40f4ac7fd5e8b4ce30ff
msgid ":ref:`NET_P1_PORT<NET_P1_PORT>` = 37260 <- this is the port that Gimbal listens for commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:103
#: 968c7548a7d4404e9d85b59d2fe12c24
msgid ":ref:`NET_P1_PROTOCOL<NET_P1_PROTOCOL>` = 8 <- Gimbal serial protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:105
#: c8c482d2ca60409bbb41c5b9c1be0d9e
msgid "Now gimbal/camera commands from the autopilot (MAVLink or AUX functions translated to SIYI commands) will be sent to the SIYI gimbal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:108
#: ad3fa142e8d54e60ace12dc22842ecba
msgid "Telemetry Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:109
#: b9cc7db12de0463090b6eebe435664ca
msgid "In order to display telemetry and communicate MAVLink commands to/from the GCS app running on the Herelink ground controller, we must set up a MAVLink path from the autopilot to Herelink air unit. We will use another \"virtual\" serial port (NET_P2) on Ethernet to talk from/to the autopilot to/from the Herelink air unit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:111
#: bab112befa72413b8a9d5f0f336e43d2
msgid ":ref:`NET_P2_TYPE<NET_P2_TYPE>` = 1 <-UDP Client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:113
#: e2216e0b65814dbbaf9c455a0d15ae66
msgid "rebooot for the params to show:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:115
#: da9f2d9030564a34b0b1c417065f0c47
msgid ":ref:`NET_P2_IP0<NET_P2_IP0>` = 192"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:116
#: 9fb39425eda84c7183ab80508c948e85
msgid ":ref:`NET_P2_IP1<NET_P2_IP1>` = 168"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:117
#: 556aaca07af644e6943a64b1c32d9bfd
msgid ":ref:`NET_P2_IP2<NET_P2_IP2>` = 144"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:118
#: cf64c8bdc9ba42a6b463592b17af8faa
msgid ":ref:`NET_P2_IP3<NET_P2_IP3>` = 11 <- this is the IP address of the Herelink air unit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:119
#: 23d86b5081514146ba9cb4990fa9e4cb
msgid ":ref:`NET_P2_PORT<NET_P2_PORT>` = 14550 <- on this port"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:120
#: 07f6f68ebfa147658f36fe7614755fed
msgid ":ref:`NET_P2_PROTOCOL<NET_P2_PROTOCOL>` = 2 <- using MAVLink2 protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ethernet-vehicle.rst:122
#: bb075d69e1ea4ef39486d22f17e1db8d
msgid "now telemetry will be sent to/from the Herelink ground unit. Opening the GCS app on the ground controller should automatically connect to the UDP telemetry stream."
msgstr ""

